# What `docker build` may see. Both Dockerfiles build from the repository root, so everything
# not listed here is sent to Docker: leaving things out keeps builds fast and secrets out.

# Installed and built inside the image (the laptop's would be the wrong OS, or stale).
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.next
**/*.tsbuildinfo
apps/web/next-env.d.ts
apps/api/data

# Secrets: production reads them from the host's env file at run time (DESIGN.md §14.4).
.env
.env.*

# Not needed to build or run the apps.
.git
.github
.vscode
**/test
**/coverage
**/*.log
**/*.md
docs
docker-compose.yml
